%% POS Offline Operations Sequence Diagram
%% Task: I3.T6
%% References: docs/pos/offline.md, Architecture §3.19.10, §3.2.9
%%
%% This diagram shows the complete POS offline flow from transaction capture
%% through encryption, queue storage, sync trigger, server replay, and audit logging.

sequenceDiagram
    actor Staff
    participant POS as POS Client
    participant SW as Service Worker
    participant IDB as IndexedDB
    participant API as Backend API
    participant Queue as POS Job Queue
    participant Worker as Background Worker
    participant Checkout as CheckoutService
    participant Payment as PaymentProvider
    participant Audit as Audit Log
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    %% === PHASE 1: Device Pairing (Prerequisites) ===
    Note over Staff,DB: Phase 1: Device Pairing (One-time Setup)

    Staff->>+API: POST /admin/api/pos/devices<br/>{name, location, model}
    API->>DB: Create device record, generate pairing code
    Note right of DB: 8-char code, 15min expiry
    API-->>-Staff: {pairingCode, expiresAt}

    Staff->>+POS: Enter pairing code in POS Settings
    POS->>+API: POST /api/pos/devices/pair<br/>{pairingCode}
    API->>DB: Validate code, generate AES-256 key
    Note right of DB: Key version increments,<br/>SHA-256 hash stored
    API->>API: Generate Stripe Terminal token (24h TTL)
    API-->>-POS: {deviceId, encryptionKey, terminalToken, keyVersion}
    POS->>IDB: Store encryptionKey in IndexedDB
    Note right of IDB: Key never sent to server<br/>after initial pairing
    POS-->>-Staff: Device paired successfully

    %% === PHASE 2: Offline Detection ===
    Note over POS,SW: Phase 2: Offline Detection & Activation

    POS->>+SW: Register background sync<br/>(pos-sw.js)
    SW->>SW: Monitor network connectivity
    Note right of SW: Triggers on:<br/>- navigator.onLine=false<br/>- fetch() timeout >10s

    alt Network offline
        SW-->>POS: offline event
        POS->>POS: Activate offline mode
        Note over POS: UI changes:<br/>- Header badge → orange "Offline"<br/>- Pulsing animation<br/>- Queue count visible
        POS->>Staff: Toast: "Network offline - transactions queued"
    end

    %% === PHASE 3: Offline Transaction Capture ===
    Note over Staff,IDB: Phase 3: Offline Transaction Capture & Encryption

    Staff->>+POS: Process sale<br/>(scan items, apply discounts, select payment)
    POS->>POS: Generate idempotency key<br/>{deviceId}:{localTxId (UUID)}
    Note right of POS: localTxId collision probability:<br/>1 in 2^122 (UUIDs)

    POS->>IDB: Retrieve encryptionKey & keyVersion

    POS->>+POS: Encrypt transaction payload
    Note over POS: AES-256-GCM encryption:<br/>- IV: 12 bytes random per transaction<br/>- Encrypted fields: cart, payment, customer PII<br/>- Plaintext: amount (metrics), idempotencyKey (dedup)
    POS-->>-POS: {encryptedPayload, iv, keyVersion}

    POS->>IDB: INSERT INTO offline_queue<br/>{idempotencyKey, encryptedPayload, iv, keyVersion, timestamp, amount, status=Queued}
    Note right of IDB: Storage limit: 50MB<br/>Alert at 100 transactions
    POS-->>-Staff: "Sale queued for sync"<br/>Print receipt with "PENDING SYNC" watermark

    %% === PHASE 4: Queue Visibility ===
    Note over Staff,IDB: Staff Queue Management (Optional)

    Staff->>+POS: Navigate to POS → Offline Queue
    POS->>IDB: SELECT * FROM offline_queue<br/>ORDER BY timestamp ASC
    IDB-->>POS: Queue entries with status
    POS-->>-Staff: Display list:<br/>- Local TX ID, timestamp, amount, staff initials<br/>- Status: Queued (orange), Syncing (blue), Failed (red)

    %% === PHASE 5: Network Restoration & Sync Trigger ===
    Note over SW,API: Phase 5: Network Restoration & Sync Trigger

    SW->>SW: Detect network restored
    Note right of SW: Triggers:<br/>- navigator.onLine=true<br/>- fetch() success<br/>- Manual "Sync Now" button<br/>- Scheduled background sync (5min)
    SW->>+POS: online event

    POS->>POS: Update UI: "Syncing X of Y transactions"
    Note over POS: Progress bar in header

    POS->>IDB: SELECT * FROM offline_queue<br/>WHERE status=Queued
    IDB-->>POS: Batch of encrypted transactions

    loop For each transaction in batch
        POS->>IDB: UPDATE status=Syncing<br/>WHERE idempotencyKey={key}
    end

    POS->>+API: POST /api/pos/offline/upload<br/>{deviceId, transactions: [{idempotencyKey, encryptedPayload, iv, keyVersion}]}
    Note right of API: Batch upload endpoint

    %% === PHASE 6: Server-side Queue & Background Job ===
    Note over API,Queue: Phase 6: Server-side Enqueue

    API->>DB: Validate deviceId & tenant authorization
    API->>DB: Check idempotency keys for duplicates
    Note right of DB: pos_offline_queue table

    alt Duplicate detected
        API-->>POS: {status=skipped, reason="Already processed"}
        POS->>IDB: UPDATE status=Skipped<br/>Mark as "Already Synced"
    else New transaction
        API->>DB: INSERT INTO pos_offline_queue<br/>{deviceId, idempotencyKey, encryptedPayload, iv, keyVersion, status=pending}
        API->>Queue: Enqueue background job<br/>Priority: DEFAULT
        Note right of Queue: pos.offline_sync queue<br/>Dispatch interval: 3s
        API-->>-POS: {status=accepted}
        POS->>IDB: Keep status=Syncing until job confirms
        POS-->>-SW: Batch upload complete
    end

    %% === PHASE 7: Background Decryption & Replay ===
    Note over Worker,Payment: Phase 7: Background Job Processing

    Worker->>+Queue: Poll for next job
    Queue-->>-Worker: POSOfflineSyncJobPayload

    Worker->>DB: SELECT device encryption key hash<br/>WHERE device_id={deviceId}
    Worker->>DB: SELECT encryptedPayload, iv, keyVersion<br/>FROM pos_offline_queue

    Worker->>+Worker: Decrypt payload using device key
    Note right of Worker: AES-256-GCM decryption:<br/>- Verify auth tag<br/>- Extract cart, payment, customer
    Worker-->>-Worker: Decrypted transaction data

    Worker->>+Checkout: createOrder(cart, customer, tenantId)
    Note right of Checkout: Standard checkout flow:<br/>- Inventory reservation<br/>- Tax calculation<br/>- Order creation
    Checkout->>DB: INSERT INTO orders<br/>{tenantId, customerId, totalAmount, status=pending}
    Checkout-->>-Worker: {orderId, orderNumber}

    Worker->>+Payment: capturePayment(orderId, paymentMethodId, amount)<br/>Idempotency-Key: {idempotencyKey}
    Note right of Payment: Stripe API call with<br/>idempotency key prevents<br/>duplicate charges

    alt Payment success
        Payment-->>Worker: {chargeId, status=succeeded}
        Worker->>DB: UPDATE orders SET status=completed<br/>WHERE order_id={orderId}
        Worker->>DB: UPDATE pos_offline_queue<br/>SET status=synced, synced_at=NOW()
        Worker->>+Audit: Log sync success
        Audit->>DB: INSERT INTO pos_offline_transactions<br/>{deviceId, orderId, idempotencyKey, syncedAt}
        Audit->>DB: INSERT INTO pos_activity_log<br/>{deviceId, action=sync_success, tenantId}
        Audit-->>-Worker: Audit complete

        Worker->>Queue: Mark job complete
        Note right of Worker: Metrics:<br/>pos.offline_sync.sync.success{device,tenant}

    else Payment failure
        Payment--xWorker: PaymentException<br/>(declined, insufficient funds, etc.)
        Worker->>Queue: Retry with exponential backoff<br/>(1s, 2s, 4s) - max 3 attempts

        alt Max retries exceeded
            Worker->>DB: UPDATE pos_offline_queue<br/>SET status=failed, error_message={details}
            Worker->>+Queue: Move to DeadLetterQueue
            Queue->>DB: INSERT INTO dead_letter_queue<br/>owning_module='pos.offline_sync'
            Queue-->>-Worker: DLQ acknowledged
            Note right of Worker: Metric:<br/>pos.offline_sync.sync.failed{error_type}

            Worker->>+Audit: Log sync failure
            Audit->>DB: INSERT INTO pos_activity_log<br/>{deviceId, action=sync_failed, error}
            Audit-->>-Worker: Audit complete
        end
    end

    Worker-->>-Payment: Processing complete

    %% === PHASE 8: Client Notification & Cleanup ===
    Note over POS,IDB: Phase 8: Client Notification & Cleanup

    API->>+POS: Server-sent event or webhook<br/>{idempotencyKey, status, orderId}
    Note right of API: Real-time update via SSE or polling

    alt Status: Synced
        POS->>IDB: UPDATE status=Synced<br/>WHERE idempotencyKey={key}
        POS->>POS: Show green checkmark
        POS->>Staff: Toast: "Transaction synced successfully"
        POS->>IDB: DELETE FROM offline_queue<br/>WHERE status=Synced AND synced_at < NOW() - 5 minutes
        Note right of IDB: Auto-cleanup after 5min

    else Status: Failed
        POS->>IDB: UPDATE status=Failed, error={message}
        POS->>POS: Show red error icon
        POS->>Staff: Toast: "Sync failed - review queue"
        Note over Staff: Staff can:<br/>- Retry sync<br/>- Export for support<br/>- Contact support
    end

    POS->>POS: Update header indicator<br/>"Online - All synced"
    POS-->>-Staff: Sync complete

    %% === PHASE 9: Staff Export (Troubleshooting) ===
    Note over Staff,IDB: Phase 9: Staff Export for Support (Optional)

    opt Queue stuck or errors
        Staff->>+POS: Click "Export Queue"
        POS->>IDB: SELECT * FROM offline_queue
        IDB-->>POS: All queue entries (encrypted)
        POS->>POS: Generate JSON export<br/>offline-queue-[timestamp].json
        POS-->>-Staff: Download file
        Note over Staff: Warning: Contains encrypted<br/>payment data - handle securely
    end

    %% === ERROR SCENARIOS ===
    Note over Worker,Audit: Error Scenarios & Alerts

    alt Encryption key lost/rotated
        Worker->>Worker: Decryption fails (wrong key version)
        Worker->>DB: UPDATE status=failed<br/>error="Key version mismatch - re-pair device"
        Worker->>Audit: Log key rotation issue
        Note right of Worker: Staff must re-pair device<br/>Old queue cannot be decrypted
    end

    alt Queue capacity exceeded
        POS->>IDB: Check storage quota
        alt Quota > 80%
            POS->>Staff: Critical alert:<br/>"Queue near capacity - sync required"
            Note right of POS: Metric: pos.offline_queue.depth{device}>100
        end

        alt Quota full (50MB)
            POS->>Staff: Error: "Cannot queue - storage full"
            POS->>POS: Suspend offline mode
            Note right of POS: Emergency fallback:<br/>Manual credit card terminal
        end
    end

    alt Device not paired
        Staff->>POS: Attempt offline transaction
        POS->>IDB: Check for encryptionKey
        alt Key not found
            POS-->>Staff: Error: "Device not paired"<br/>Navigate to Settings → Device Pairing
        end
    end

    %% === KILL SWITCH & FEATURE FLAGS ===
    Note over API,Worker: Kill Switch via Feature Flags

    opt Kill switch activated
        API->>DB: Check FeatureToggle("pos.offline.enabled")
        alt Flag disabled
            API-->>POS: HTTP 503 Service Unavailable<br/>"POS offline mode temporarily disabled"
            POS->>Staff: Toast: "Offline mode unavailable"
        end

        Worker->>DB: Check FeatureToggle("pos.offline_sync.enabled")
        alt Flag disabled
            Worker->>Worker: Skip job processing, requeue
            Note right of Worker: Stops sync without failing jobs
        end
    end

    %% === MONITORING ANNOTATIONS ===
    Note over Queue,Audit: Key Metrics & Alerts

    Note right of Queue: Metrics:<br/>- pos.offline_queue.depth{device_id}<br/>- pos.offline_sync.sync.success{device,tenant}<br/>- pos.offline_sync.sync.failed{error_type}<br/>- pos.offline_sync.job.duration (p95)<br/><br/>Alerts:<br/>- Queue depth >100 for 10min (P2)<br/>- Sync failure rate >10% for 5min (P2)<br/>- Device offline >4 hours (P3)<br/>- Queue capacity >80% (P1)
